0..77 Comment "// Access at a place. `access xs[i] as w { … }` lends one element of a held"
78..155 Comment "// list to a view: the index is a value read where the access stands, and the"
156..234 Comment "// view is the element at it. An exclusive view writes its element back at its"
235..310 Comment "// index and the rest of the list stands as it was; a shared view reads it."
311..387 Comment "// The held list is lent as a whole, whatever the index, so two views of one"
388..462 Comment "// list stand together only when both are shared. The place follows Rust\'s"
463..539 Comment "// index expression on a place (_The Rust Reference_, § Index expressions)."
541..611 Comment "/// The list each access below holds; a list\'s type is declared, never"
612..625 Comment "/// inferred."
626..628 Other "@["
629..633 Other "runs"
